Job Description
We are looking for a highly motivated Junior Business Analyst in our fast-growing Private Markets Platform team. The team brings together expertise in Business Analysis, Business Architecture, and Project Management, and plays a central role in shaping how the firm operates at scale. Our focus is on driving large-scale transformations, improving end-to-end processes, and designing scalable, future-ready solutions that support our clients and investment teams.
What you will do
Designing, re-engineering and documenting key business processes with different stakeholders on business and IT side;
Conducting requirement analysis and detailed gap assessments on a wide range of topics across the company;
Writing test cases, organise and perform User Acceptance Testing (UAT);
Supporting in project management activities, such as organising workshops with SMEs, overseeing IT delivery, preparing status reports and resource & work planning;
Defining and presenting conceptual approaches (orally and in writing), target operating models, preparing solution options and required decisions, and documenting results;
Closely working with IT counterparts to bridge between business and technology teams;
Training business users on rolled-out tools, push for adoption and support the entire change management process.
We are looking for individuals who
Are curious and intellectually engaged, with a genuine interest in understanding complex and evolving business models;
Naturally ask “why”, challenge assumptions, and seek to understand root causes rather than symptoms;
Are comfortable challenging the status quo in a constructive and thoughtful way;
Have a strong desire to learn quickly, especially in new and unfamiliar domains and take ownership.
Requirements
University degree or equivalent, qualifying experience in Business Economics, Business Informatics or Information Technology;
First working experience of business analysis in a financial services company or with a leading consulting firm in a similar hands-on role at the interface between Business and IT;
Motivation to work on own initiative and in collaboration with various stakeholders, ability to deliver on time with a high level of integrity;
Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to understand business and technical functions as well as process information quickly;
Must be comfortable with constructively challenging the status quo and looking for new ways to improve processes and results;
Great team player and ability to work collaboratively at various levels of the organization;
Excellent communication and presentation skills in written and verbal English.
Contact Information
If you are interested in becoming an integral part of a successful alternative investment management team in an international, multicultural working environment we will be pleased to get to know you soon.
For further information please contact us.
Aline de Montmollin
Human Resources
LGT Capital Partners (U.K.) Ltd.
Contact
+41 58 261 81 60

Chiyu Banking Corporation Limited has been registered as a licensed bank since 1947. Rooted in Hong Kong, we strive to provide one-stop cross-border banking and financial services to customers in Hong Kong, mainland and overseas Chinese. Riding on the edge of the Hong Kong and Fujian business and our cross-border platform, we will continuously maintain its core values of “Sincerity, Flexibility, Tailor-made Service and Professionalism” and provide premium services to our customers to help growing their wealth, and to create values and deliver returns to our stakeholders and staff.
We believe that employees are valuable asset of the company. We offer stimulating careers that will further your personal growth. Come join us for the following position.
Responsibilities
Business & System Analysis: Understand and explain complex business processes, systems, and tools, with a specific focus on the business logic analysis of Hong Kong payment systems (e.g.FPS, CHATS, SWIFT); deeply understand function and impact of payment system and related system;
Cross-Departmental Liaison: Act as a bridge between business users and technical developers to ensure that business requirements for payment systems and other related systems are well-defined and accurately implemented;
Project Advancement & Risk Management: Assist in the concrete implementation and delivery of projects; proactively manage potential risks throughout the project development lifecycle, and recommend appropriate mitigation measures when necessary;
Testing & Version Management: Responsible for system testing and product version management;
Requirements
Bachelor Degree holder in Computer Science or related disciplines;
HKIB banking professional qualifications such as Enhanced Competency Framework (ECF) and/or Certified Banker (CB) preferred;
3 to 5 years of relevant experience in system development and implementation, with at least 2 years in business analysis or system analysis role, and a proven track record in business requirement discussions and documentation;
Familiar with the local financial and payment systems in Hong Kong; proficient in the operational workflows and development of FPS, CHATS, and SWIFT systems;
Possess hands-on project development, system maintenance, system analysis experience in Linux environments and Oracle DB;
Solid experience in handling tasks and documentation in the full SDLC, system testing (SIT & UAT), and Version Control Management;
Strong analytical and report-writing skills; proven analytical skills in writing the business requirement document and functional specification document;
Proactive, able to work independently and under pressure;
Well-versed written and verbal English and Chinese (both Cantonese and Mandarin).
We offer competitive packages and promising career opportunities to the right candidates. Please send your full resume with current salary, expected salary and the date of availability to
Human Resources Department, Chiyu Banking Corporation Ltd, 8/F, Chiyu Bank Building, No. 78 Des Voeux Road Central, Central, Hong Kong
or fax to
2986-3233
or by clicking
Apply Now
.
Information provided will be treated in strict confidence and only be used for recruitment purposes. All personal data of unsuccessful applicants will be destroyed after the recruitment exercise. A copy of Personal Information Collection Statement is available upon request.

Description de l'entreprise
Notre organisation, située dans la région métropolitaine de Montréal propose des services professionnels en Ingénieire et en Sciences de la Vie par le biais de ses consultants. Nous couvrons des segments de marché tel que l'industrie Pharmaceutique, Agroalimentaire, Cosmétiques, des Dispositifs Médicaux et des Technologies de l'Information et des Communications (TIC).
Sans toutefois être exhaustives, les compétences couvertes par nos consultants englobent les activités suivantes:
Secteurs des TIC
Architecture et réseaux TI;
Analyse TI;
Assurance qualité;
Cybersécurité;
Développement des logiciels;
Programmation;
Gestion des projets TI;
Etc.
Secteurs des Sciences de la Vie
Ingénierie (Projet, Maintenance, Procédés, Bâtiments, etc.);
Validation;
Assurance qualité;
Affaires réglementaires;
Pharmacovigilance;
Rédaction technique;
HSE;
Etc.
Description de l’offre d’emploi
Description Du Poste
FOP CONSULTANTS est à la recherche d’
Analystes d’affaires
motivé à la réalisation de mandats. Les principales missions seraient d’analyser les besoins et les processus d’affaires, de recueillir et de prioriser les exigences, de proposer des solutions et des optimisations de processus, de soutenir les essais et la conduite du changement et d’assurer le lien entre les parties prenantes et les équipes TI.
RESPONSABILITÉS PRINCIPALES
Recueillir, analyser et prioriser les besoins et les exigences d’affaires.
Cartographier les processus actuels et cibles et identifier les possibilités d’optimisation.
Produire les dossiers d’affaires, les analyses d’écarts et les recommandations de solution.
Rédiger les exigences, les récits utilisateurs et les critères d’acceptation.
Mobiliser les parties prenantes et faciliter les ateliers de travail.
Soutenir les essais d’acceptation, la formation et la conduite du changement.
Assurer le lien entre les parties prenantes d’affaires et les équipes TI.
PROFIL RECHERCHÉ
Diplôme universitaire en informatique, gestion ou toutes disciplines connexes.
Cinq (05) à dix (10) années d’expérience en technologie de l’information.
Trois (03) à sept (07) années d’expérience comme analyste d’affaires.
Expérience avec l’un des cadre suivants : Scrum, Kanban, Lean, DSDM, SAFe, Nexus.
Détenir l’une des certifications suivantes : ECBA, PMI-PBA.
Détenir l’une des certifications suivantes (atout) : CBAP, CBA, PROSCI ADKAR.
Expérience avec l’un des outils suivants : Azure DevOps, JIRA, Confluence.
Expérience dans les organismes publics ou privés du Canada.
Langue : Français
MODE DE TRAVAIL
Télétravail, hybride, sur site
CE QUE NOUS OFFRONS
Chez FOP CONSULTANTS, Nous Investissons Dans Le Succès Et Le Bien-être De Nos Experts. En Vous Joignant à Notre Équipe, Vous Bénéficiez D’un Environnement Conçu Pour Soutenir Votre Performance Et Respecter Votre Équilibre De Vie, Notamment
Une rémunération compétitive, à la hauteur de votre expertise;
Une protection complète grâce à nos assurances collectives;
Une assurance professionnelle pour pratiquer en toute confiance;
La flexibilité du travail à distance, selon les besoins du client;
3 semaines de vacances pour recharger vos batteries;
3 jours de congés maladie payés, pour prendre soin de vous;
De réelles possibilités d’avancement au sein de l’organisation;
Un accès continu à la formation pour faire évoluer vos compétences.
Qualifications professionnellesCette offre d'emploi est soumise à une qualification professionnelle reconnue en dehors du réseau scolaire ou universitaire : (certificats, permis, cours, appartenance à un ordre ou une association professionnelle, etc.)Langues
Français parlé et écrit - Élevé
Formations
Baccalauréat 1er cycle, Informatique - Informatique et recherche opérationnelle
Baccalauréat 1er cycle, Informatique - Informatique et gestion
